---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroCanvas from '../components/HeroCanvas.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How this site handles your data.">
  <section class="relative flex min-h-[50dvh] items-center px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-text">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mt-2">How this site handles your data.</p>
    </div>
    <HeroCanvas animation="cipher" />
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-text space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        This site uses <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> and the <strong>LinkedIn Insight Tag</strong>, both gated
        behind a consent banner. No tracking occurs before you grant consent. When analytics is enabled, aggregate
        traffic data (page views, scroll depth, reading time) and basic device context (language, timezone, screen size)
        are collected. No data is sold. Data is shared only with Google (GA4) and LinkedIn (Insight Tag) for analytics
        purposes.
      </p>
      <h2>Local Storage &amp; Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        Two items are stored in your browser's <strong>localStorage</strong> (not cookies): a theme preference (<code
          >theme</code
        >) and a visit counter (<code>adrianwedd_visits</code>). Your analytics consent choice is also stored in
        localStorage (<code>adrianwedd_consent</code>). These persist until you clear your browser data.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        If you grant consent, GA4 and LinkedIn set their own cookies for analytics tracking. These are third-party
        cookies managed by Google and LinkedIn respectively.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        Questions about privacy? <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
